WEBVTT

00:08.820 --> 00:15.580
In the deepest darkness lie the sleeping butterflies.

00:16.970 --> 00:23.520
Are they even aware of the blue sky?

00:25.130 --> 00:28.550
The world is fragile, like building blocks.

00:28.680 --> 00:32.530
I want a way to fly away.

00:32.890 --> 00:36.260
I pray for only one thing

00:36.740 --> 00:40.650
for the one that I love.

00:42.430 --> 00:46.380
Now, the dices were thrown.

00:46.440 --> 00:50.390
Paradise will rise in the future.

00:50.410 --> 00:54.580
You and I Tooi yumeni musubareru

00:50.410 --> 00:54.580
You and I will unite in this far away dream.

00:54.700 --> 00:58.430
And we will cross this red river.

00:58.490 --> 01:02.230
The flower embraces the cross with uncertainty.

01:02.490 --> 01:06.390
Like that, bloomed a fickle angel.

01:06.390 --> 01:10.460
We will one day find eternal love

01:10.710 --> 01:14.760
and I will give you Paradise.

01:34.340 --> 01:36.760
It's so noisy I can't sleep.

02:16.900 --> 02:17.750
Musica.

02:19.130 --> 02:20.620
We're ready.

02:21.040 --> 02:26.490
Silver Rhythm's Musica

02:55.800 --> 02:58.060
Oh! That was a good pass!

02:58.060 --> 02:59.220
Look! Yeah!

02:59.250 --> 03:00.760
There! Shoot!

03:01.340 --> 03:03.720
Ah, almost!

03:03.800 --> 03:05.440
Their finish is always bad!

03:05.680 --> 03:07.940
Do it right this time, ok?

03:08.310 --> 03:10.510
Good! Keep going!

03:41.520 --> 03:42.940
Alright! Good!

03:42.980 --> 03:43.860
Hey, there!

04:02.090 --> 04:04.300
They better score in the second half.

04:05.840 --> 04:06.420
What's wrong?

04:06.720 --> 04:07.470
Oh, nothing.

04:08.180 --> 04:10.340
I thought I saw something on the screen.

04:10.640 --> 04:11.260
What?

04:14.770 --> 04:16.140
You must be imagining things.

04:16.180 --> 04:17.310
Yeah...

04:17.980 --> 04:19.480
Huh? Who's that?

04:19.810 --> 04:20.900
Is he stupid or what?

04:21.770 --> 04:22.690
Yeah.

04:23.900 --> 04:25.570
An intruder?!

05:55.070 --> 05:55.870
Let's go.

05:56.160 --> 05:56.870
What?!

05:57.370 --> 05:58.410
Withdraw.

05:59.830 --> 06:02.170
But the money is right in front of us.

06:08.090 --> 06:09.590
Idiot, hurry up and get out.

06:15.090 --> 06:16.550
It's not here either.

06:24.150 --> 06:25.690
Huh? It's not here.

06:32.070 --> 06:32.740
What?

06:32.900 --> 06:35.280
Musica, same as always?

06:35.620 --> 06:37.160
Sure, leave it.

06:37.240 --> 06:38.450
Roger.

06:39.740 --> 06:45.630
It's even a piece of cake for Silver Rhythm
to break into the National Casino vault.

06:46.920 --> 06:47.420
Huh?

07:00.600 --> 07:02.810
Musica, something is wrong.

07:03.640 --> 07:04.640
Hebi, what happened?

07:04.850 --> 07:08.940
P-Pl-Pl-Plue is in my backpack.

07:13.320 --> 07:14.990
Hebi failed.

07:16.300 --> 07:17.800
Hey!

07:18.850 --> 07:20.240
Plue!

07:20.240 --> 07:22.290
I wonder where he went?

07:22.410 --> 07:23.750
Musica isn't here either.

07:23.780 --> 07:24.660
Hey, Haru!

07:25.220 --> 07:26.010
Musica.

07:26.080 --> 07:28.170
Sorry, Plue got caught.

07:28.330 --> 07:29.630
What?! How?!

07:30.130 --> 07:32.670
Seems like he tagged along with us.

07:32.710 --> 07:33.840
Really?!

07:34.010 --> 07:34.840
Don't worry.

07:35.050 --> 07:36.300
I'll definitely get him back.

07:36.470 --> 07:37.590
I'll help too!

07:37.720 --> 07:39.280
This is my responsibility.

07:39.390 --> 07:41.260
You can count on me to get Plue back.

07:41.600 --> 07:43.600
Nobody interfere.

07:48.520 --> 07:50.560
What?! Oh man!

07:50.770 --> 07:52.570
Poor Plue!

07:53.730 --> 07:55.150
Stupid raccoon.

07:55.440 --> 07:56.720
I told you it's a bug!

07:56.760 --> 07:57.460
It's a dog, isn't it?

07:57.990 --> 08:00.620
It doesn't matter, what are you going to do?

08:03.330 --> 08:07.000
He's the leader of Silver Rhythm.

08:07.330 --> 08:10.040
Why don't you leave it to him?

08:10.290 --> 08:11.130
But!

08:11.250 --> 08:13.610
He's not facing the Demon Cards.

08:13.640 --> 08:15.970
So you shouldn't be fighting against them.

08:17.930 --> 08:21.350
You broke into the vault and you didn't steal anything?!

08:21.510 --> 08:26.020
That's what I've been saying!

08:26.350 --> 08:27.810
Where are your friends?

08:28.100 --> 08:29.350
What are you talking about?

08:29.520 --> 08:32.020
Are you saying that you and that... um...

08:32.610 --> 08:33.610
It's kinda like a dog.

08:33.820 --> 08:37.990
That dog alone, broke into the National Casino vault?

08:38.070 --> 08:39.040
Yes.

08:39.070 --> 08:44.370
I was walking with him and we somehow
ended up in this casino.

08:44.910 --> 08:46.000
I wonder what happened?

08:47.120 --> 08:48.660
Then what's this?

08:49.000 --> 08:51.420
It was found in the vault.

08:51.630 --> 08:52.420
What is it?

08:53.040 --> 08:56.710
Liar! You're a member of Silver Rhythm, aren't you?

08:57.130 --> 08:57.630
Huh?

08:58.300 --> 09:01.890
I'm asking if you're a member of the Silver Rhythm,

09:02.050 --> 09:05.390
that recently broke into sixteen casinos and banks.

09:05.930 --> 09:08.140
What on earth are you talking about?!

09:08.180 --> 09:10.350
Friends and bandits, you say?

09:11.310 --> 09:12.230
That's fine.

09:12.860 --> 09:15.570
By the way, what's its name?

09:16.030 --> 09:16.980
Plue.

09:17.780 --> 09:19.900
I see, Plue, huh?

09:20.490 --> 09:22.570
Is this a horn or a nose?

09:25.580 --> 09:27.120
Cute!

09:30.210 --> 09:32.630
Hey, don't take us so lightly.

09:33.420 --> 09:35.910
We finally have a lead on Silver Rhythm.

09:35.960 --> 09:38.590
I'll spend a lot of time interrogating you for details.

09:38.760 --> 09:40.050
Be ready for it!

09:40.680 --> 09:42.390
Will I be able to handle it?

09:43.510 --> 09:44.470
Sir!

09:45.220 --> 09:46.890
I'm questioning him right now.

09:47.060 --> 09:50.890
A man who calls himself the leader of
Silver Rhythm just turned himself in.

09:51.060 --> 09:52.800
What?!

09:55.980 --> 09:57.940
Musica turned himself in.

09:59.740 --> 10:02.110
Sorry, Musica.

10:02.240 --> 10:04.620
It's because I screwed up.

10:17.460 --> 10:20.970
<i>Just minutes ago, a man who called himself
the leader of Silver Rhythm was arrested.</i>

10:21.720 --> 10:26.680
<i>Silver Rhythm is a group of bandits who
robbed many casinos and banks.</i>

10:22.620 --> 10:24.280
Look, look, it's Musica!

10:26.970 --> 10:30.350
<i>Authorities are investigating if he is
linked to the other recent crimes.</i>

10:30.930 --> 10:32.980
He's pretty famous, isn't he?

10:33.560 --> 10:35.770
I wonder what he's going to do.

10:37.190 --> 10:38.730
Making himself look so cool.

10:43.150 --> 10:45.320
He takes after my bad genes.

10:45.490 --> 10:45.870
Eh?

10:56.420 --> 10:57.580
Musica.

10:59.170 --> 11:02.800
Big brother! I... I...

11:02.840 --> 11:03.970
It's okay.

11:04.090 --> 11:06.640
I won't abandon my friends.

11:07.970 --> 11:10.850
Since I was little, I've always been alone. So...

11:10.970 --> 11:12.850
Eh? Really?

11:13.230 --> 11:13.890
Yeah.

11:14.350 --> 11:16.190
What about your family?

11:17.400 --> 11:19.320
That's what you promised not to ask, right?

11:19.610 --> 11:20.860
Y-yes.

11:21.280 --> 11:22.320
By the way...

11:23.280 --> 11:27.990
Seems like they don't know that I can control silver.

11:28.240 --> 11:29.620
Lucky!

11:31.700 --> 11:33.540
Ah, this is tasty!

11:34.830 --> 11:38.290
Hey, old man, I've been thinking about this for a while.

11:38.720 --> 11:42.630
You and the other Musica are actually related, aren't you?

11:43.300 --> 11:47.680
That's right. You both have the same last name, Musica.

11:49.680 --> 11:51.100
Isn't that right, old man?

11:56.440 --> 11:57.140
I don't know.

11:59.150 --> 12:00.940
Wait! Hey, what is that?

12:02.980 --> 12:03.980
This is...

12:04.400 --> 12:06.450
I didn't notice that until now.

12:06.610 --> 12:08.070
Hey, old man, that's...

12:08.240 --> 12:09.700
This is nothing.

12:10.450 --> 12:11.870
Right now

12:12.700 --> 12:15.040
it doesn't mean anything anymore.

12:25.420 --> 12:29.390
Hey, did you know that the leader of
Silver Rhythm turned himself in?

12:29.720 --> 12:32.850
Yeah, I heard that he's locked up in a cell.

12:42.230 --> 12:45.490
Ah! My nightshift is finally over.

12:45.940 --> 12:49.410
My wife isn't happy because
I've been coming home so late.

12:49.570 --> 12:52.580
I've been working hard but she doesn't understand.

12:52.990 --> 12:54.430
Yeah, but that's what makes her cute.

13:07.300 --> 13:09.590
Speaking of which, what are you
going to do with those two?

13:09.760 --> 13:11.510
The members of Silver Rhythm?

13:11.720 --> 13:13.970
I'll start a thorough interrogation on them tomorrow.

13:14.260 --> 13:15.430
This is bad.

13:15.510 --> 13:18.770
There is not even single person, who was interrogated
by me and have not told the truth yet!

13:20.980 --> 13:24.820
There's a reason why my nickname is 'Demon'.

13:28.570 --> 13:30.310
Oh, what is it?

13:32.110 --> 13:33.950
You lost your way, huh?

13:35.490 --> 13:39.000
I see. I see. Do you want to have
some milk or something inside?

13:39.030 --> 13:39.830
Excuse me.

13:40.250 --> 13:41.280
What is it?

13:41.790 --> 13:45.920
That's what I locked in the cell with
the two members of Silver Rhythm.

13:46.050 --> 13:47.920
Who told you to do such a thing?!

13:48.170 --> 13:50.840
This guy's innocent you know?

13:50.880 --> 13:52.930
That's not what I'm saying.

13:53.090 --> 13:54.010
Then what is it?

13:54.090 --> 13:56.850
This was in the cell with the two of them.

13:57.060 --> 13:58.600
Poor thing, huh?

14:01.020 --> 14:02.060
What?!

14:02.140 --> 14:04.900
Are you saying that those two escaped?!

14:04.930 --> 14:06.730
That's what I've been saying.

14:06.760 --> 14:08.530
Shit! Call everyone!

14:09.190 --> 14:11.030
Runaways!

14:15.990 --> 14:17.700
We owe you one, Plue.

14:19.080 --> 14:20.500
Musica, hurry.

14:22.710 --> 14:25.170
We should be okay here.

14:26.000 --> 14:28.830
No, here isn't good either.

14:29.340 --> 14:31.980
Listen, they must be still around here.

14:32.050 --> 14:34.860
You must find them. Don't even let a cat out of this area!

14:35.140 --> 14:35.890
Idiot!

14:35.930 --> 14:38.600
You think that you can escape from this town?

14:42.430 --> 14:44.650
They are everywhere.

14:45.850 --> 14:48.020
We need to contact out guys.

14:48.570 --> 14:51.740
They took out cell phones.

14:53.450 --> 14:54.240
Huh? What is it?

14:55.910 --> 14:58.020
What? Are you hungry?

14:58.490 --> 15:00.990
This isn't the time to eat.

15:01.030 --> 15:02.260
Hebi, let's go!

15:02.300 --> 15:03.500
Wa-wait.

15:04.040 --> 15:08.790
<i>A moment ago, we announced that two bandits
from Silver Rhythm were arrested,</i>

15:08.910 --> 15:11.210
<i>but just now they escaped from their cells.</i>

15:11.460 --> 15:15.930
<i>Authorities now have over 200
policemen searching for them.</i>

15:22.600 --> 15:23.390
Hey, wait!

15:23.640 --> 15:25.600
Hey! Over here!

15:27.270 --> 15:29.480
I've found one of the fugitives, I'm at...

15:29.880 --> 15:30.730
Musica.

15:30.730 --> 15:32.110
I talked to our guys.

15:32.360 --> 15:35.450
We will carry out plan B at the intersection ahead.

15:35.610 --> 15:36.490
Good.

15:37.570 --> 15:39.800
Don't worry. We're going be fine.

15:40.060 --> 15:41.540
There they are!

15:42.120 --> 15:44.200
Both of them!

15:44.870 --> 15:45.830
Don't let them get away.

15:48.580 --> 15:49.790
Wait!

15:59.600 --> 16:00.620
Where are they?

16:00.970 --> 16:02.650
They were just here, huh?

16:02.930 --> 16:03.810
They are gone.

16:04.350 --> 16:07.180
Shit! We were chasing the wrong ones.

16:12.320 --> 16:13.980
I got Plue back, just like I said.

16:14.360 --> 16:15.440
Where are you going?

16:15.690 --> 16:17.860
We can't stay in this town.

16:18.070 --> 16:19.320
See you again some day.

16:19.530 --> 16:20.530
Wait!

16:20.700 --> 16:21.240
Huh?

16:21.370 --> 16:23.450
You already noticed, didn't you?

16:23.580 --> 16:25.120
Who that old man is.

16:25.450 --> 16:26.620
What are you talking about?

16:26.830 --> 16:28.040
Don't pretend like you don't know!

16:28.250 --> 16:31.790
You and that old man are related, aren't you?

16:32.380 --> 16:34.510
I can feel it somehow.

16:35.380 --> 16:37.090
Even if we're, what does it matter?

16:37.300 --> 16:39.300
Why are you leaving without saying anything to him?

16:39.550 --> 16:41.890
You guys at one point both thought
that your families were dead,

16:42.350 --> 16:43.970
but one of them is still alive!

16:44.810 --> 16:47.100
Aren't you misunderstanding something?

16:47.180 --> 16:48.090
Misunderstand?

16:48.390 --> 16:50.770
You say that the blacksmith is my grandpa?

16:51.610 --> 16:55.360
Even if it's true, I'm not going to tell him!

16:55.680 --> 16:56.490
Why not?

16:56.570 --> 16:58.070
His grandson is a bandit.

16:58.490 --> 16:59.860
How can he be happy with that?

17:00.360 --> 17:01.790
That's not true!

17:01.820 --> 17:05.490
The old man thinks that his entire family is gone.

17:05.740 --> 17:08.620
He'll be happy just knowing that
one of them is still alive.

17:10.170 --> 17:11.960
I wish it was as simple as that.

17:12.430 --> 17:14.290
There's another reason why I won't tell him.

17:14.750 --> 17:19.220
If I say that I'm his grandson, the old
man's life will be held back by me.

17:19.260 --> 17:22.050
My life will also be held back by him.

17:22.340 --> 17:23.550
I don't want that.

17:24.010 --> 17:25.060
What are you talking about?

17:25.810 --> 17:29.940
Besides, there's still something I need to do!

17:30.770 --> 17:32.400
It's going to be fine like this.

17:32.650 --> 17:34.110
I don't get it!

17:34.270 --> 17:35.520
Being held back you say?!

17:35.690 --> 17:39.820
How can it be so complicated to say "I'm alive"?!

17:39.990 --> 17:42.780
We've both thought that our families were
dead, and suddenly one appeared...

17:42.910 --> 17:44.700
Only to go separate ways soon anyways.

17:44.740 --> 17:47.410
There are things better left unsaid.

17:47.580 --> 17:49.290
It's just one line though!

17:50.210 --> 17:52.120
That "I'm alive".

17:52.250 --> 17:54.210
He's the only one left in your family, right?!

17:58.210 --> 18:00.130
What's this racket?

18:01.930 --> 18:03.680
I heard you guys talking.

18:04.340 --> 18:06.100
You said that he's my grandson?

18:06.260 --> 18:07.480
I think he is.

18:09.760 --> 18:13.400
I told you my family was killed before my eyes.

18:13.520 --> 18:14.190
But.

18:14.810 --> 18:16.700
What about your past?

18:17.940 --> 18:18.980
I was picked up

18:19.480 --> 18:22.400
by a man called Silver Claimer Rize.

18:23.740 --> 18:28.040
Over a decade ago, my family was murdered.

18:28.950 --> 18:34.540
Rize who happened to pass by,
picked me up and raised me.

18:34.830 --> 18:35.960
The only survivor.

18:36.900 --> 18:38.130
A family murdered...

18:38.880 --> 18:41.880
Wasn't Lance the one who did that?

18:42.340 --> 18:44.720
Old man! Musica! You guys must be the only survivors!

18:44.750 --> 18:46.930
I guess it's possible.

18:47.100 --> 18:50.480
I was too sad to check if they were all dead

18:50.650 --> 18:52.640
and I didn't even hold a funeral for them.

18:53.100 --> 18:55.100
I didn't care anymore.

18:55.730 --> 19:01.690
But if you really are a Musica, there
should be a crest on your right arm.

19:02.820 --> 19:04.110
The same one as this.

19:04.910 --> 19:06.990
Musica, show us your right arm.

19:08.910 --> 19:09.870
No way.

19:10.490 --> 19:11.950
He doesn't have the crest. That means.

19:13.040 --> 19:14.410
That's right.

19:14.920 --> 19:18.210
You and I are totally unrelated.

19:18.420 --> 19:20.130
I guess so.

19:20.380 --> 19:21.660
Musica!

19:21.840 --> 19:23.520
Let's go now!

19:23.720 --> 19:26.640
I've got news about the thing we've been looking for.

19:26.800 --> 19:27.730
What?

19:27.760 --> 19:29.220
I'll give you the details later.

19:29.300 --> 19:31.180
I'm going now! Take care!

19:35.350 --> 19:37.750
Old man, I'll visit you some day.

19:38.690 --> 19:40.070
Don't die till then, ok?

19:40.860 --> 19:41.820
Fool!

19:42.230 --> 19:44.050
Don't say such stupid things!

19:44.740 --> 19:45.660
Old man.

19:45.820 --> 19:48.320
He is your grandson, isn't he?

19:48.910 --> 19:49.620
Yes.

19:50.370 --> 19:54.120
He is definitely my grandson, Hamrio Musica!

19:54.790 --> 19:55.900
Then how come?!

19:56.000 --> 19:58.380
I heard you guys talking.

19:58.790 --> 20:03.090
I don't want to be a burden
for someone who's traveling the world.

20:03.420 --> 20:05.470
We don't have to agree with each other.

20:05.720 --> 20:08.430
I'm happy enough just knowing he is alive.

20:22.610 --> 20:25.140
See you again some day, grandpa!

20:26.280 --> 20:28.910
Thank you for fixing my sword.

20:29.410 --> 20:31.820
Thank you for a lot of things too.

20:31.830 --> 20:33.450
I don't know how to repay you.

20:33.620 --> 20:35.180
I'm happy for you too, old man,

20:35.410 --> 20:36.840
although I don't know what's going on.

20:37.540 --> 20:39.220
Where are you going now?

20:39.300 --> 20:41.250
I need to find four more Raves,

20:41.340 --> 20:43.990
but I don't know what to do.

20:44.170 --> 20:47.840
Shiba told me that Plue would lead
me in the right direction,

20:48.720 --> 20:49.930
but he's being like this.

20:51.550 --> 20:54.890
I don't know if this will help you,

20:55.140 --> 20:57.970
but how about looking for them
in the Land of Falling Stars?

20:58.390 --> 20:59.700
Land of Falling Stars?

20:59.920 --> 21:01.650
That sounds pretty!

21:02.020 --> 21:09.070
After overdrive 50 years ago, Rave
dispersed throughout the world.

21:09.570 --> 21:16.700
It was around noon when I saw a shooting
star that landed to the north.

21:17.250 --> 21:24.420
If that shooting star was one of the dispersed
Raves, there must be other people who saw it.

21:24.630 --> 21:31.590
If you ask around, you should be able to make it
to the place where the star landed, "Rave Point".

21:31.800 --> 21:32.710
I see!

21:32.800 --> 21:34.240
Then I might be able to find it!

21:34.260 --> 21:35.760
I'm not totally sure.

21:35.850 --> 21:38.980
Don't forget that this is only a clue.

21:39.250 --> 21:39.920
Alright!

21:39.980 --> 21:41.790
My destination is somewhere up north!

21:41.830 --> 21:42.770
The Land of Falling Stars!

21:42.810 --> 21:44.110
It's settled then!

21:45.570 --> 21:49.740
There are a lot of monsters in the north, so be careful.

21:49.950 --> 21:52.240
Alright, I will. I'm going now!

21:56.760 --> 21:58.910
Mysterious kid.

21:59.250 --> 22:02.920
He might be able to lead our world to peace.

22:04.250 --> 22:07.200
Do your best! Rave Master, Haru!

22:13.620 --> 22:23.950
Under the moon, I became a chrysalis, kissed upon a glass sea of love.

22:23.950 --> 22:33.890
Your rhythm is like a wave, embraced by the words of its song.

22:33.890 --> 22:44.020
Live to feel me, my past disappears on the water's surface.

22:44.520 --> 22:54.630
Everything I believed in, I found with you, so...

22:54.630 --> 23:04.860
You're wings on my heart kono negai haruka na yume no shijima ni tokete

22:54.630 --> 23:04.860
You're the wings on my heart, this wish, a distant dream that melts on a deserted island.

23:04.860 --> 23:18.780
All I want is for the bluebird to lead me to you, and drift through the country.

23:19.060 --> 23:26.030
Toward the small sky that weeps.

23:41.470 --> 23:42.820
Alright, to the north!

23:43.090 --> 23:44.530
Let's go to the land of Falling Stars!

23:44.610 --> 23:46.540
But how do we get there?

23:46.570 --> 23:47.800
Leave it to me Haru!

23:47.840 --> 23:49.230
